WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.760
From client brief, to clear quotation, to portfolio.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:12.050
This is the video for module four of Interior Decoration Basics: client brief, quotation and your decorating business.

3
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:20.740
A weak brief causes most disputes. I said modern, not this. A strong brief makes every later decision easier.

4
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:26.300
A clear quotation protects both sides and shows professionalism.

5
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.070
Good payment terms keep your own money safe.

6
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:37.290
And clients hire decorators whose work they can see, so your portfolio is your strongest sales tool.

7
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:50.490
Ask the client to send two or three photos of the room by WhatsApp. For your safety, tell someone where you are going and when you expect to finish, especially when visiting a new client alone.

8
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.970
At the visit, ask what the room is for, who uses it, what they dislike now, and which items must stay.

9
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:13.600
Ask about style, colours, budget and timeline. When a client says modern or cosy, ask her to point to a picture, because those words mean different things to different people. If she is shy about budget, offer ranges.

10
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.950
If the client rents, check that the landlord allows painting or drilling.

11
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:34.060
After the visit, type the brief in short points and send it: please confirm this is correct. Keep the reply. If the client later asks for a second room, treat it as a change request with its own price and timeline.

12
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:40.110
Let us build Oluchi's quote, line by line. These are illustrative figures.

13
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:50.620
Materials: curtain fabric, lining, paint, bulbs, a lamp and cushion covers come to 102,550 naira.

14
00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:57.310
Labour for other trades, the painter, tailoring and track fitting, is 53,000.

15
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.920
Transport and delivery, 10,000. Beginners often forget their own transport.

16
00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:13.490
Her own design and coordination fee is a fixed 60,000, on its own line, so the client sees what she pays Oluchi for.

17
00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:20.710
Contingency is 10% of materials and labour, rounded to 15,600.

18
00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:33.030
The total is 241,150 naira, with every part on a separate line. A single total with no breakdown invites suspicion and bargaining.

19
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:40.530
Write the scope: what is included, and what is not, such as electrical work by the client's electrician.

20
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.580
Say the quote is valid for 14 days, because prices change.

21
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:54.210
Ask for a deposit before you buy materials, and confirm it in your bank app, not by SMS alert, before you shop.

22
00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:58.640
Give a start date and a finish date, and what could delay it.

23
00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:12.540
And state that extra work is quoted separately and approved in writing. If the total is over budget, do not just cut your fee. Offer a cheaper fabric, a feature wall, or doing the work in phases.

24
00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:30.240
Build three to six projects, each with the brief in two lines, before and after pairs, and the colour scheme. A floor plan or mood board shows you plan properly. Decorating a relative's parlour or a church office for photos and a testimonial counts.

25
00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:39.360
Never post faces or the address without permission, and never write fake reviews. One discovered fake can destroy trust.

26
00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:51.570
Ruth turned one parlour makeover in Jos into five posts. Day one, a before and after pair. Day two, the floor plan and how moving the sofa freed the walkway.

27
00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:58.120
Day three, the colour scheme. Day four, a 30-second video of the curtains opening.

28
00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:08.710
Day five, the client's testimonial, with a line inviting people to book. Each post teaches something, and brings enquiries without paid adverts.

29
00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:26.170
To remember. Confirm the brief in writing. Put your fee on its own line. Add materials, labour, transport, fee and contingency. Take the deposit first and confirm it in your bank app. And show only real work and real testimonials.

30
00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:42.950
Now practise. Run a practice brief with a friend and make a mood board. Write a full quotation with real prices, 10% contingency and terms. Then launch your portfolio and your WhatsApp Business profile, and complete your capstone.

31
00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.240
Continue with the lessons below.
